@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJyb2xlIjoiQURNSU4iLCJuYW1lIjoiSmFzb24iLCJzdWIiOiJhZG1pbkBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTc4Njc3MDA2NiwiZXhwIjoxNzg2ODU2NDY2fQ.UeQ4o5nYmfRmn4DVMfZbTiqn0HDT4ZyQK_qu7D6zdy0

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### 2. Readiness check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/readiness

### 3. Protected endpoint without token - should return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets

### 4. Login as admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}

### 5. Protected endpoint with token - should return 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Paged tickets timing check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=id&direction=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Invalid sort field - should return 400 if validation is enabled
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=password&direction=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Report timing check: tickets by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/tickets-by-status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Report timing check: tickets by priority
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/tickets-by-priority
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Duplicate ticket or invalid payload check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Duplicate Network Issue",
  "description": "Unable to connect to internal Wi-Fi",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "admin@example.com"
}

### 11. Trigger 403 Forbidden (User role attempting Admin action)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unauthorized Create Attempt",
  "description": "User role trying to post to admin route",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "LOW"
}

### 12. Trigger 404 Not Found (Non-existent ticket ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Trigger 409 Conflict (Duplicate ticket resource)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Duplicate Ticket Ref",
  "description": "Triggering unique constraint error",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "admin@example.com"
}